  summary: Corn is actually a giant grass! Each ear is wrapped up in leafy husks.
  facts:
  - People in southern Mexico first grew corn about 10,000 years ago!
  - Each strand of corn silk leads to just one kernel!
  - Corn kernels can be red, blue, pink or even black!
  - Popcorn pops because heat makes the water inside each kernel expand until it
    bursts!
  sources:
  - Encyclopaedia Britannica. Corn. https://www.britannica.com/plant/corn-plant
